// A slur that spans a grace note, on a notation + TAB pair. On the tab staff a
// slur connects fret DIGITS on their string lines, so it must arch ABOVE the
// numbers — clearing the encompassed main-note digits AND the small grace digit
// hanging off them. A pitch-based arc (the notation slur scorer) ran straight
// through those digits; the tab slur is laid out directly against the fret rows.
title "Tab Grace Slur"
composer "Lily#"

part bl { clef bass tuning bass }
section A {
  bl { c4\4( grace { d16 } e4\3) f4\4( grace { g16 } a4\3) | }
}
form main { A }
score main "tab-grace-slur" {
  staff bl
  tab bl
}
